	)
	(text "Three Raspberry Pi Pico 2 modules, USB Type-C socket, links"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12 14 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3 3)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "addf5855-6efc-5d3c-a9da-a923c1da4537")
	)
	(text "power switch of the Famicom half, and reprogramming of Pico A and Pico B through their debug pads."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12 35 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "a97143a7-6a64-5984-b619-32a6f3d312d5")
	)
	(text "Pico A (video): clock and reset for CPU and PPU, palette index and sprite bit in, RGB and sync out; the emulator in emulation mode."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12 20 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "d0c40440-f121-534b-bbe8-6b961cd877b4")
	)
	(text "Pico C (input/output and management): JAMMA inputs and outputs, coin and timer logic, cartridge dump, USB Type-C,"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12 30 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "766f15fa-caff-50b8-aba7-97b3339e7806")
	)
	(text "The modules are soldered flat on the board.  The USB socket reaches Pico C through the pads under the module (TP2, TP3)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12 40 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "3307748e-a4dd-5eed-89d2-f893c0da2080")
	)
	(text "Pico B (bus): watches the CPU's accesses to the PPU, replaces palette data on the PPU side, answers the controller reads."
